IMPORT `coa-core`
IMPORT `coa23-nouns`

-- coa23-part35-registrar.l4: Companies Act 2006 (United Kingdom), Part 35 (The registrar of companies), ss 1059A to 1071,
-- lines 14867-15079 of ukpga-2006-46.txt. Layer 1: the law, objectively, from the text alone.
--
-- SOURCE. A plain-text rendering of the Act from legislation.gov.uk made by a converter script; it is not the
-- official text and nothing here is "verified against the official text". Quote lines are checked by srcrefs.py.
--
-- HOW TO READ AN ANSWER (the rule of 2026-10-29, assumed, not ruled by a lawyer; see NOTES.md).
--   JUST TRUE / JUST FALSE / NOTHING as in coa-definitions.l4: a "no" only where the text says no in its own words
--   (a "means" definition; "if", "only if", "where", "unless"; a flat negative; a period it fixes), and NOTHING
--   everywhere else (silent, list not closed, includes, undefined term, points outside the text, limited by its
--   own wording). Each branch that says no carries -- FALSE-kind (...); each that says "not covered" carries
--   -- NOTHING-kind (...). A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
-- A bare "must" that is not done is answered JUST FALSE in a function named for compliance (fork F5).
-- Seam inputs are named as inputs/PLAN.md section 4 names them. Every top-level name begins with its section label.

§ `Part 35 - The registrar of companies: ss 1059A to 1071`

§§ `s 1059A Scheme of this Part`

-- s 1059A(1) ("The scheme of this Part is as follows.") only introduces the lists: inert (reason 1, a lead-in; fork F6).

DECLARE `s 1059A way a provision of this Part applies` IS ONE OF
    `s 1059A(2) generally (to the registrar, to any functions of the registrar, or to documents delivered to or issued by the registrar under any enactment, as the case may be)`
    `s 1059A(3) in relation to companies (to companies or for the purposes of the Companies Acts, as the case may be)`
    `s 1059A(4) as indicated in the provisions concerned`

-- A section is named by its number, the letter that follows it (A, B, ... or the empty string) and, where the list
-- names only some subsections of it, the subsection (1, 2, ...; the empty string for the whole section). The key puts
-- 1062A between 1062 and 1063, so that a range such as "sections 1061 to 1063" takes in 1062A.
-- src:14869 | 1059A Scheme of this Part
-- src:14870 | (1) The scheme of this Part is as follows.
-- src:14871 | (2) The following provisions apply generally (to the registrar, to any functions of the registrar, or to documents delivered to or issued by the registrar under any enactment, as the case may be)—
-- src:14872 | sections 1060(1) and (2) and 1061 to 1063 (the registrar),
-- src:14873 | sections 1068 1067A to 1071 (delivery of documents to the registrar),
-- src:14874 | sections 1072 to 1076 (requirements for proper delivery),
-- src:14875 | sections 1080(1), (4) and (5) and 1092 (keeping and production of records),
-- src:14876 | section 1081A (registrar’s objectives to promote integrity of registers etc),
-- src:14877 | section 1083 (preservation of original documents),
-- src:14878 | section 1084A (recording optional information on register),
-- src:14879 | sections 1092A to 1092C (powers to require further information),
-- src:14880 | sections 1108 to 1110 (language requirements: transliteration),
-- src:14881 | sections 1110E to 1110G (disclosure of information),
-- src:14882 | sections 1111 and 1114 to 1119 (supplementary provisions).
-- src:14883 | section 1112B (false statement offences: national security etc defence).
-- src:14884 | (3) The following provisions apply in relation to companies (to companies or for the purposes of the Companies Acts, as the case may be)—
-- src:14885 | section 1060(3) and (4) (references to the registrar in the Companies Acts),
-- src:14886 | sections 1064 and 1065 (certificates of incorporation),
-- src:14887 | section 1066 (companies' registered numbers),
-- src:14888 | sections 1077 to 1079A (public notice of certain information),
-- src:14889 | sections 1080(2) and (3), 1081 , 1082 and 1084 (the register),
-- src:14890 | sections 1085 to 1091 (inspection of the register),
-- src:14891 | sections 1093 to 1098 (correction or removal of material on the register),
-- src:14892 | sections 1098A to 1098H (authorised corporate service providers),
-- src:14893 | section 1106 (voluntary filing of translations),
-- src:14894 | sections 1110A and 1110B (identity verification),
-- src:14895 | sections 1112, 1112A and 1113 (enforcement).
-- src:14896 | (4) The following provisions apply as indicated in the provisions concerned—
-- src:14897 | section 1067 (registered numbers of UK establishments of overseas companies),
-- src:14898 | sections 1099 to 1101 (the registrar's index of company names),
-- src:14899 | sections 1102 to 1105 and 1107 (language requirements: translation).
-- src:14900 | section 1110C (identity verification: exemption on national security grounds),
-- src:14901 | section 1110D (power to require businesses to report discrepancies),
@ref s 1059A(2) to (4) Scheme of this Part: how each listed provision applies (src:14869-14901)
GIVEN `the number of the section` IS A NUMBER
      `the letter that follows the number, or the empty string` IS A STRING
      `the subsection, or the empty string for the whole section` IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 1059A way a provision of this Part applies`
`s 1059A(2) to (4) how the provision of this Part applies` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- row 2.1 sections 1060(1) and (2) and 1061 to 1063 (line 14872)
        IF (key AT LEAST 1060 AND key AT MOST 1060 AND (`the subsection, or the empty string for the whole section` EQUALS "1" OR `the subsection, or the empty string for the whole section` EQUALS "2")) OR (key AT LEAST 1061 AND key AT MOST 1063) THEN JUST `s 1059A(2) generally (to the registrar, to any functions of the registrar, or to documents delivered to or issued by the registrar under any enactment, as the case may be)`
        -- row 2.2 sections 1068 1067A to 1071 (the text reads 1067A to 1071: fork F3) (line 14873)
        IF (key AT LEAST 1067.01 AND key AT MOST 1071) THEN JUST `s 1059A(2) generally (to the registrar, to any functions of the registrar, or to documents delivered to or issued by the registrar under any enactment, as the case may be)`
        -- row 2.3 sections 1072 to 1076 (line 14874)
        IF (key AT LEAST 1072 AND key AT MOST 1076) THEN JUST `s 1059A(2) generally (to the registrar, to any functions of the registrar, or to documents delivered to or issued by the registrar under any enactment, as the case may be)`
        -- row 2.4 sections 1080(1), (4) and (5) and 1092 (line 14875)
        IF (key AT LEAST 1080 AND key AT MOST 1080 AND (`the subsection, or the empty string for the whole section` EQUALS "1" OR `the subsection, or the empty string for the whole section` EQUALS "4" OR `the subsection, or the empty string for the whole section` EQUALS "5")) OR (key AT LEAST 1092 AND key AT MOST 1092) THEN JUST `s 1059A(2) generally (to the registrar, to any functions of the registrar, or to documents delivered to or issued by the registrar under any enactment, as the case may be)`
        -- row 2.5 section 1081A (line 14876)
        IF (key AT LEAST 1081.01 AND key AT MOST 1081.01) THEN JUST `s 1059A(2) generally (to the registrar, to any functions of the registrar, or to documents delivered to or issued by the registrar under any enactment, as the case may be)`
        -- row 2.6 section 1083 (line 14877)
        IF (key AT LEAST 1083 AND key AT MOST 1083) THEN JUST `s 1059A(2) generally (to the registrar, to any functions of the registrar, or to documents delivered to or issued by the registrar under any enactment, as the case may be)`
        -- row 2.7 section 1084A (line 14878)
        IF (key AT LEAST 1084.01 AND key AT MOST 1084.01) THEN JUST `s 1059A(2) generally (to the registrar, to any functions of the registrar, or to documents delivered to or issued by the registrar under any enactment, as the case may be)`
        -- row 2.8 sections 1092A to 1092C (line 14879)
        IF (key AT LEAST 1092.01 AND key AT MOST 1092.03) THEN JUST `s 1059A(2) generally (to the registrar, to any functions of the registrar, or to documents delivered to or issued by the registrar under any enactment, as the case may be)`
        -- row 2.9 sections 1108 to 1110 (line 14880)
        IF (key AT LEAST 1108 AND key AT MOST 1110) THEN JUST `s 1059A(2) generally (to the registrar, to any functions of the registrar, or to documents delivered to or issued by the registrar under any enactment, as the case may be)`
        -- row 2.10 sections 1110E to 1110G (line 14881)
        IF (key AT LEAST 1110.05 AND key AT MOST 1110.07) THEN JUST `s 1059A(2) generally (to the registrar, to any functions of the registrar, or to documents delivered to or issued by the registrar under any enactment, as the case may be)`
        -- row 2.11 sections 1111 and 1114 to 1119 (line 14882)
        IF (key AT LEAST 1111 AND key AT MOST 1111) OR (key AT LEAST 1114 AND key AT MOST 1119) THEN JUST `s 1059A(2) generally (to the registrar, to any functions of the registrar, or to documents delivered to or issued by the registrar under any enactment, as the case may be)`
        -- row 2.12 section 1112B (line 14883)
        IF (key AT LEAST 1112.02 AND key AT MOST 1112.02) THEN JUST `s 1059A(2) generally (to the registrar, to any functions of the registrar, or to documents delivered to or issued by the registrar under any enactment, as the case may be)`
        -- row 3.1 section 1060(3) and (4) (line 14885)
        IF (key AT LEAST 1060 AND key AT MOST 1060 AND (`the subsection, or the empty string for the whole section` EQUALS "3" OR `the subsection, or the empty string for the whole section` EQUALS "4")) THEN JUST `s 1059A(3) in relation to companies (to companies or for the purposes of the Companies Acts, as the case may be)`
        -- row 3.2 sections 1064 and 1065 (line 14886)
        IF (key AT LEAST 1064 AND key AT MOST 1065) THEN JUST `s 1059A(3) in relation to companies (to companies or for the purposes of the Companies Acts, as the case may be)`
        -- row 3.3 section 1066 (line 14887)
        IF (key AT LEAST 1066 AND key AT MOST 1066) THEN JUST `s 1059A(3) in relation to companies (to companies or for the purposes of the Companies Acts, as the case may be)`
        -- row 3.4 sections 1077 to 1079A (line 14888)
        IF (key AT LEAST 1077 AND key AT MOST 1079.01) THEN JUST `s 1059A(3) in relation to companies (to companies or for the purposes of the Companies Acts, as the case may be)`
        -- row 3.5 sections 1080(2) and (3), 1081, 1082 and 1084 (line 14889)
        IF (key AT LEAST 1080 AND key AT MOST 1080 AND (`the subsection, or the empty string for the whole section` EQUALS "2" OR `the subsection, or the empty string for the whole section` EQUALS "3")) OR (key AT LEAST 1081 AND key AT MOST 1082) OR (key AT LEAST 1084 AND key AT MOST 1084) THEN JUST `s 1059A(3) in relation to companies (to companies or for the purposes of the Companies Acts, as the case may be)`
        -- row 3.6 sections 1085 to 1091 (line 14890)
        IF (key AT LEAST 1085 AND key AT MOST 1091.99) THEN JUST `s 1059A(3) in relation to companies (to companies or for the purposes of the Companies Acts, as the case may be)`
        -- row 3.7 sections 1093 to 1098 (line 14891)
        IF (key AT LEAST 1093 AND key AT MOST 1098) THEN JUST `s 1059A(3) in relation to companies (to companies or for the purposes of the Companies Acts, as the case may be)`
        -- row 3.8 sections 1098A to 1098H (line 14892)
        IF (key AT LEAST 1098.01 AND key AT MOST 1098.08) THEN JUST `s 1059A(3) in relation to companies (to companies or for the purposes of the Companies Acts, as the case may be)`
        -- row 3.9 section 1106 (line 14893)
        IF (key AT LEAST 1106 AND key AT MOST 1106) THEN JUST `s 1059A(3) in relation to companies (to companies or for the purposes of the Companies Acts, as the case may be)`
        -- row 3.10 sections 1110A and 1110B (line 14894)
        IF (key AT LEAST 1110.01 AND key AT MOST 1110.02) THEN JUST `s 1059A(3) in relation to companies (to companies or for the purposes of the Companies Acts, as the case may be)`
        -- row 3.11 sections 1112, 1112A and 1113 (line 14895)
        IF (key AT LEAST 1112 AND key AT MOST 1112.01) OR (key AT LEAST 1113 AND key AT MOST 1113) THEN JUST `s 1059A(3) in relation to companies (to companies or for the purposes of the Companies Acts, as the case may be)`
        -- row 4.1 section 1067 (line 14897)
        IF (key AT LEAST 1067 AND key AT MOST 1067) THEN JUST `s 1059A(4) as indicated in the provisions concerned`
        -- row 4.2 sections 1099 to 1101 (line 14898)
        IF (key AT LEAST 1099 AND key AT MOST 1101) THEN JUST `s 1059A(4) as indicated in the provisions concerned`
        -- row 4.3 sections 1102 to 1105 and 1107 (line 14899)
        IF (key AT LEAST 1102 AND key AT MOST 1105) OR (key AT LEAST 1107 AND key AT MOST 1107) THEN JUST `s 1059A(4) as indicated in the provisions concerned`
        -- row 4.4 section 1110C (line 14900)
        IF (key AT LEAST 1110.03 AND key AT MOST 1110.03) THEN JUST `s 1059A(4) as indicated in the provisions concerned`
        -- row 4.5 section 1110D (line 14901)
        IF (key AT LEAST 1110.04 AND key AT MOST 1110.04) THEN JUST `s 1059A(4) as indicated in the provisions concerned`
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the section is not in any of the three lists
    WHERE
        key MEANS `the number of the section` PLUS letterValue
        letterValue MEANS
            BRANCH
                IF `the letter that follows the number, or the empty string` EQUALS "" THEN 0
                IF `the letter that follows the number, or the empty string` EQUALS "A" THEN 0.01
                IF `the letter that follows the number, or the empty string` EQUALS "B" THEN 0.02
                IF `the letter that follows the number, or the empty string` EQUALS "C" THEN 0.03
                IF `the letter that follows the number, or the empty string` EQUALS "D" THEN 0.04
                IF `the letter that follows the number, or the empty string` EQUALS "E" THEN 0.05
                IF `the letter that follows the number, or the empty string` EQUALS "F" THEN 0.06
                IF `the letter that follows the number, or the empty string` EQUALS "G" THEN 0.07
                IF `the letter that follows the number, or the empty string` EQUALS "H" THEN 0.08
                OTHERWISE 0.5

-- src:14902 | (5) Unless the context otherwise requires, the provisions of this Part apply to an overseas company as they apply to a company as defined in section 1.
@ref s 1059A(5) The provisions of this Part and an overseas company (src:14902)
GIVEN `the context otherwise requires` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1059A(5) the provision of this Part applies to the overseas company as it applies to a company as defined in section 1` MEANS
    IF `the context otherwise requires`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Unless the context otherwise requires" reserves the context without saying what applies then (fork F7: an "unless" once met)
    ELSE JUST TRUE

§§ `s 1060 The registrar`

-- src:14905 | (1) There shall continue to be—
-- src:14906 | (a) a registrar of companies for England and Wales,
-- src:14907 | (b) a registrar of companies for Scotland, and
-- src:14908 | (c) a registrar of companies for Northern Ireland.
@ref s 1060(1) There shall continue to be a registrar of companies for each part (src:14905-14908)
GIVEN place IS A `Place of registration`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1060(1) there is to continue to be a registrar of companies for the place` MEANS
    CONSIDER place
    WHEN `England and Wales` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `Scotland` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `Northern Ireland` THEN JUST TRUE

-- s 1060(2) (the registrars are appointed by the Secretary of State) is an office and its staffing: inert (reason 2).

-- src:14910 | (3) In the Companies Acts“the registrar of companies” and “the registrar” mean the registrar of companies for England and Wales, Scotland or Northern Ireland, as the case may require.
@ref s 1060(3) "the registrar of companies" and "the registrar" (src:14910)
GIVEN `the place the case requires` IS A `Place of registration`
GIVETH A `s 1060 registrar of companies`
`s 1060(3) the registrar of companies, as the case may require, for the place` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the place the case requires`
    WHEN `England and Wales` THEN `s 1060(1)(a) the registrar of companies for England and Wales`
    WHEN `Scotland` THEN `s 1060(1)(b) the registrar of companies for Scotland`
    WHEN `Northern Ireland` THEN `s 1060(1)(c) the registrar of companies for Northern Ireland`

-- src:14911 | (4) References in the Companies Acts to registration in a particular part of the United Kingdom are to registration by the registrar for that part of the United Kingdom.
@ref s 1060(4) Registration in a particular part of the United Kingdom (src:14911)
GIVEN `the part of the United Kingdom` IS A `Place of registration`
GIVETH A `s 1060 registrar of companies`
`s 1060(4) registration in the part of the United Kingdom is registration by` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the part of the United Kingdom`
    WHEN `England and Wales` THEN `s 1060(1)(a) the registrar of companies for England and Wales`
    WHEN `Scotland` THEN `s 1060(1)(b) the registrar of companies for Scotland`
    WHEN `Northern Ireland` THEN `s 1060(1)(c) the registrar of companies for Northern Ireland`

§§ `s 1061 The registrar's functions`

-- src:14913 | (1) The registrar shall continue—
-- src:14914 | (a) to perform the functions conferred on the registrar by or under the Companies Acts or any other enactment, and
-- src:14915 | (b) to perform such functions on behalf of the Secretary of State, in relation to the registration of companies or other matters, as the Secretary of State may from time to time direct.
@ref s 1061(1) The registrar's functions: what the registrar shall continue to do (src:14913-14915)
GIVEN `the function is conferred on the registrar by or under the Companies Acts or any other enactment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary of State has directed the registrar to perform the function on the Secretary of State's behalf in relation to the registration of companies or other matters` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1061(1) the registrar must perform the function` MEANS
    IF       `the function is conferred on the registrar by or under the Companies Acts or any other enactment`
        OR   `the Secretary of State has directed the registrar to perform the function on the Secretary of State's behalf in relation to the registration of companies or other matters`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(a) to perform the functions conferred on the registrar by or under the Companies Acts or any other enactment, and (b) to perform such functions on behalf of the Secretary of State ... as the Secretary of State may from time to time direct"

-- s 1061(2) is blank in this text.

-- src:14917 | (3) References in this Act to the functions of the registrar are to functions within subsection (1)(a) or (b).
@ref s 1061(3) The functions of the registrar (src:14917)
GIVEN `the function is conferred on the registrar by or under the Companies Acts or any other enactment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the function is one the Secretary of State has directed the registrar to perform on the Secretary of State's behalf` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1061(3) the function is a function of the registrar for the purposes of the Act` MEANS
    IF       `the function is conferred on the registrar by or under the Companies Acts or any other enactment`
        OR   `the function is one the Secretary of State has directed the registrar to perform on the Secretary of State's behalf`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "References in this Act to the functions of the registrar are to functions within subsection (1)(a) or (b)"

§§ `s 1062 The registrar's official seal`

-- src:14919 | The registrar shall have an official seal for the authentication of documents in connection with the performance of the registrar's functions.
@ref s 1062 The registrar's official seal (src:14919)
GIVEN `the seal is the official seal the registrar has` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it authenticates a document in connection with the performance of the registrar's functions` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1062 the document bears the registrar's official seal` MEANS
    IF `the seal is the official seal the registrar has` AND `it authenticates a document in connection with the performance of the registrar's functions`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): section 1062 gives the registrar a seal for authentication and says nothing of any other seal or other use

§§ `s 1062A Analysis of information for the purposes of crime prevention or detection`

-- src:14921 | (1) The registrar must carry out such analysis of information within the registrar’s possession as the registrar considers appropriate for the purposes of preventing or detecting crime.
@ref s 1062A(1) The registrar must analyse information for the purposes of preventing or detecting crime (src:14921)
GIVEN `the information is within the registrar's possession` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the registrar considers the analysis appropriate for the purposes of preventing or detecting crime` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1062A(1) the registrar must carry out the analysis` MEANS
    IF `the information is within the registrar's possession` AND `the registrar considers the analysis appropriate for the purposes of preventing or detecting crime`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "such analysis of information within the registrar’s possession as the registrar considers appropriate" (the judgment is the registrar's, taken here as an input)

-- The duty as a regulative rule. No time limit is stated, so none is invented (the rule has no WITHIN). The recipient
-- field of the generic action is a placeholder: the text names nobody to whom the analysis is owed.
@ref s 1062A(1) The registrar must analyse information (src:14921)
`s 1062A(1) the registrar's duty to analyse information` MEANS
    PARTY Registrar
    MUST `Action of a party` OF Registrar, Registrar, "analyse information within the registrar's possession for the purposes of preventing or detecting crime"

-- s 1062A(2) ("See also section 1110F") is a cross-reference only: inert (reason 1).

§§ `s 1063 Fees payable to registrar`

-- s 1063(1), (3), (3A), (4), (6A) and (6B) confer or regulate powers to make regulations (and (3A) lists what the Secretary of State
-- may take into account in doing so): inert (reason 2). s 1063(7) amends the Limited Partnerships Act 1907: inert (reason 2, amendment of another Act).

DECLARE `s 1063(2) matter for which fees may be charged` IS ONE OF
    `s 1063(2)(a) the performance of a duty imposed on the registrar or the Secretary of State`
    `s 1063(2)(b) the receipt of documents delivered to the registrar`
    `s 1063(2)(c) the inspection, or provision of copies, of documents kept by the registrar`
    `s 1063(2) another matter`

-- src:14927 | (2) The matters for which fees may be charged include—
-- src:14928 | (a) the performance of a duty imposed on the registrar or the Secretary of State,
-- src:14929 | (b) the receipt of documents delivered to the registrar, and
-- src:14930 | (c) the inspection, or provision of copies, of documents kept by the registrar.
@ref s 1063(2) The matters for which fees may be charged include (src:14927-14930)
GIVEN m IS A `s 1063(2) matter for which fees may be charged`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1063(2) fees may be charged for the matter` MEANS
    CONSIDER m
    WHEN `s 1063(2) another matter` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "The matters for which fees may be charged include"
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:14951 | (5) In respect of the performance of functions or the provision of services or facilities—
-- src:14952 | (a) for which fees are not provided for by regulations, or
-- src:14953 | (b) in circumstances other than those for which fees are provided for by regulations,
-- src:14954 | the registrar may determine from time to time what fees (if any) are chargeable.
@ref s 1063(5) The registrar may determine fees where regulations provide none (src:14951-14954)
GIVEN `fees are provided for by regulations for the function, service or circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1063(5) the registrar may determine from time to time what fees, if any, are chargeable` MEANS
    IF `fees are provided for by regulations for the function, service or circumstances`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the grant covers functions or services "for which fees are not provided for by regulations" and circumstances "other than those for which fees are provided"
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:14955 | (6) Fees received by the registrar are to be paid into the Consolidated Fund.
@ref s 1063(6) Fees received by the registrar are to be paid into the Consolidated Fund (src:14955)
GIVEN `the registrar has received the fee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the fee has been paid into the Consolidated Fund` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1063(6) the fee received by the registrar has been dealt with as the section requires` MEANS
    IF `the registrar has received the fee`
    THEN IF `the fee has been paid into the Consolidated Fund`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Fees received by the registrar are to be paid into the Consolidated Fund" (a bare "are to be" not done: fork F5)
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the section speaks only of "Fees received by the registrar"

§§ `ss 1064 and 1065 Certificates of incorporation`

-- src:14969 | (1) The registrar must cause to be published—
-- src:14970 | (a) in the Gazette, or
-- src:14971 | (b) in accordance with section 1116 (alternative means of giving public notice),
-- src:14972 | notice of the issue by the registrar of any certificate of incorporation of a company.
@ref s 1064(1) Public notice of the issue of a certificate of incorporation (src:14969-14972)
GIVEN `a certificate of incorporation of a company has been issued by the registrar` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1064(1) the registrar must cause notice of the issue of the certificate to be published` MEANS
    IF `a certificate of incorporation of a company has been issued by the registrar`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "notice of the issue by the registrar of any certificate of incorporation of a company"

@ref s 1064(1) The registrar has complied: published in the Gazette or in accordance with section 1116 (src:14969-14972)
GIVEN `the notice was published in the Gazette` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 1116 the notice was published in accordance with section 1116 (alternative means of giving public notice)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1064(1) the registrar has complied by publishing the notice` MEANS
    IF `the notice was published in the Gazette`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE CONSIDER `s 1116 the notice was published in accordance with section 1116 (alternative means of giving public notice)`
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must cause to be published— (a) in the Gazette, or (b) in accordance with section 1116" (a bare "must" not done: fork F5)
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): section 1116 is in another part's range (coa24)

-- The duty as a regulative rule (no time limit is stated). The recipient field is a placeholder.
@ref s 1064(1) The registrar must cause notice to be published (src:14969-14972)
`s 1064(1) the registrar's duty to publish notice of the issue of a certificate of incorporation` MEANS
    PARTY Registrar
    MUST `Action of a party` OF Registrar, Company, "publish notice of the issue of the certificate of incorporation"

-- src:14973 | (2) The notice must state the name and registered number of the company and the date of issue of the certificate.
