    IF `the copy is of a certificate of incorporation of a company` AND `the copy is signed by the registrar or authenticated by the registrar's seal`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any person may require the registrar to provide him with a copy of any certificate of incorporation of a company, signed by the registrar or authenticated by the registrar's seal"

-- The right as a regulative rule: any person MAY require the copy. The correlative duty of the registrar is not stated in the text.
@ref s 1065 Any person may require a copy (src:14980)
