§§ `ss 1066 and 1067 Registered numbers`

-- src:14983 | (1) The registrar shall allocate to every company a number, which shall be known as the company's registered number.
@ref s 1066(1) The registrar shall allocate to every company a registered number (src:14983)
GIVEN `s 1(1) the body is a company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1066(1) the registrar must allocate a registered number to the company` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 1(1) the body is a company`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty is to allocate "to every company" and says nothing of other bodies (section 1066(6) extends "company" for this section to some overseas companies)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the body is a company is section 1(1), which the answering part supplies

-- src:14984 | (2) Companies' registered numbers shall be in such form, consisting of one or more sequences of figures or letters, as the registrar may determine.
@ref s 1066(2) The form of registered numbers (src:14984)
GIVEN `the registered number consists of one or more sequences of figures or letters` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is in a form the registrar has determined` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1066(2) the registered number is in the form the section requires` MEANS
    IF `the registered number consists of one or more sequences of figures or letters` AND `it is in a form the registrar has determined`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Companies' registered numbers shall be in such form, consisting of one or more sequences of figures or letters, as the registrar may determine" (a bare "shall" not met: fork F5)

-- src:14985 | (3) The registrar may on adopting a new form of registered number make such changes of existing registered numbers as appear necessary.
@ref s 1066(3) The registrar may change existing numbers on adopting a new form (src:14985)
GIVEN `the registrar is adopting a new form of registered number` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the change of the existing number appears necessary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1066(3) the registrar may change the existing registered number` MEANS
    IF `the registrar is adopting a new form of registered number`
    THEN IF `the change of the existing number appears necessary`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "such changes of existing registered numbers as appear necessary"
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may on adopting a new form of registered number make such changes" ("on" counts as "when" or "upon", so a failed "on adopting" is a no: ruling of 2026-11-05 (c))

-- src:14986 | (4) A change of a company's registered number has effect from the date on which the company is notified by the registrar of the change.
@ref s 1066(4) A change of registered number has effect from the date the company is notified (src:14986)
GIVEN `the company has been notified by the registrar of the change` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date on which the company was notified` IS A DATE
      `the day in question` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1066(4) the change of registered number has effect on the day` MEANS
    IF `the company has been notified by the registrar of the change`
    THEN IF `the day in question` AT LEAST `the date on which the company was notified`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "has effect from the date on which the company is notified by the registrar of the change" (a period the text fixes in its own words: ruling of 2026-11-05 (a))
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): no date of notification yet, so the text gives no date from which the change has effect

-- src:14987 | (5) For a period of three years beginning with that date any requirement to disclose the company's registered number imposed by regulations under section 82 or section 1051 (trading disclosures) is satisfied by the use of either the old number or the new.
@ref s 1066(5) For a period of three years beginning with that date (src:14987)
GIVEN `the date from which the change has effect` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 1066(5) the last day of the three years beginning with the date` MEANS
    (Date (DATE_DAY `the date from which the change has effect`) (DATE_MONTH `the date from which the change has effect`) ((DATE_YEAR `the date from which the change has effect`) PLUS 3)) MINUS 1

@ref s 1066(5) For three years either the old or the new number satisfies a disclosure requirement (src:14987)
GIVEN `the date from which the change has effect` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the number is disclosed` IS A DATE
      `the number disclosed is the old number or the new number` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1066(5) the requirement to disclose the registered number imposed by regulations under section 82 or section 1051 is satisfied by the number disclosed` MEANS
    IF       `the day on which the number is disclosed` AT LEAST `the date from which the change has effect`
        AND  `the day on which the number is disclosed` AT MOST `s 1066(5) the last day of the three years beginning with the date` `the date from which the change has effect`
    THEN IF `the number disclosed is the old number or the new number`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): within the three years the text says only that either number satisfies; it does not say what happens to a third number
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "For a period of three years beginning with that date any requirement ... is satisfied by the use of either the old number or the new" (a period the text fixes in its own words: ruling of 2026-11-05 (a))

-- src:14988 | (6) In this section “company” includes an overseas company whose particulars have been registered under section 1046, other than a company that appears to the registrar not to be required to register particulars under that section.
@ref s 1066(6) "company" in this section includes some overseas companies (src:14988)
