      `it appears to the registrar that the company is not required to register particulars under section 1046` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1066(6) the overseas company is a company for the purposes of section 1066` MEANS
    IF `the overseas company's particulars have been registered under section 1046`
    THEN IF `it appears to the registrar that the company is not required to register particulars under section 1046`
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "other than a company that appears to the registrar not to be required to register particulars under that section" (an "(other than X)" site: fork F8)
         ELSE JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "“company” includes an overseas company whose particulars have been registered" says what is included and not what is excluded

-- src:14990 | (1) The registrar shall allocate to every UK establishment of an overseas company whose particulars are registered under section 1046 a number, which shall be known as the UK establishment's registered number.
