§§ `ss 1067A and 1067B Who may deliver documents to the registrar`

-- src:15001 | (1) An individual may not deliver a document to the registrar on their own behalf unless—
-- src:15002 | (a) their identity is verified (see section 1110A), and
-- src:15003 | (b) the document is accompanied by a statement to that effect.
@ref s 1067A(1) An individual delivering a document on their own behalf (src:15001-15003)
GIVEN `s 1110A the individual's identity is verified` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the document is accompanied by a statement that the individual's identity is verified` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1067A(1) the individual is barred from delivering the document to the registrar on their own behalf` MEANS
    IF `the document is accompanied by a statement that the individual's identity is verified`
    THEN CONSIDER `s 1110A the individual's identity is verified`
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An individual may not deliver a document ... unless— (a) their identity is verified ..., and (b) the document is accompanied by a statement to that effect" (an "unless" once met: fork F9)
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the identity is verified is section 1110A, in another part's range (coa24)
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- The bar as a regulative rule: the individual SHANT deliver on their own behalf, where the identity is not verified or no
-- statement accompanies the document (the guard says when the act is the prohibited act). No time limit is stated.
@ref s 1067A(1) The bar as a prohibition (src:15001-15003)
`s 1067A(1) the prohibition on an individual delivering a document on their own behalf` MEANS
    PARTY `s 1067A an individual who delivers a document to the registrar`
    SHANT `s 1067A deliver a document on their own behalf` verified statement PROVIDED (NOT verified) OR (NOT statement)
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `s 1067A an individual who delivers a document to the registrar` BECAUSE "the individual delivered a document on their own behalf without verified identity and a statement to that effect"

-- s 1067A(2): the table. Column 1 is B, the person on whose behalf the document is delivered; column 2 is A, the
-- individual who delivers it; column 3 is the statement that must accompany the document. Each row of the table is one function
-- (the exception to the bar that the row creates). Fork F10: B being a firm has four rows; the text says "the corresponding entry" without
-- saying how a firm's four rows combine, so any one of the firm's rows that is satisfied lifts the bar.
DECLARE `s 1067A(2) the person on whose behalf the document is delivered (B)` IS ONE OF
    `s 1067A(2) B is a firm`
    `s 1067A(2) B is an individual`

DECLARE `s 1067A(2) statement made by A` IS ONE OF
    `s 1067A(2) statement that A is an officer or employee of the firm`
    `s 1067A(2) statement that A is an officer or employee of a corporate officer of the firm`
    `s 1067A(2) statement that A is an authorised corporate service provider`
    `s 1067A(2) statement that A is an officer or employee of an authorised corporate service provider`
    `s 1067A(2) statement that A is delivering the document on the firm's behalf`
    `s 1067A(2) statement that A is delivering the document on B's behalf`
    `s 1067A(2) statement that A's identity is verified`

DECLARE `s 1067A(2) facts about the individual who delivers the document (A)` HAS
    `s 1067A(2) A is an officer or employee of the firm` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 1067A(2) A is an officer or employee of a corporate officer of the firm` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 1067A(2) A is an officer or employee of an authorised corporate service provider` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 1067A(2) A's identity is verified, the answer of section 1110A` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `s 1067A(2) A is an authorised corporate service provider, the answer of section 1098A` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN

-- A plain fact together with an answer that may be NOTHING: a failed plain fact is a no whatever the answer is.
GIVEN `the plain facts hold` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the answer of another section` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1067A(2) the plain facts hold and the answer of another section is` MEANS
    IF `the plain facts hold`
    THEN `the answer of another section`
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the row is an exception stated by "unless (a) ... and (b) ...", and a limb that fails is a no (marginal reading (a))

-- src:15009 | 1 | Firm | Individual who is an officer or employee of the firm and whose identity is verified (see section 1110A). | Statement by A—that A is an officer or employee of the firm,that A is delivering the document on the firm’s behalf, andthat A’s identity is verified.
@ref s 1067A(2) Table row 1: a firm; an officer or employee of the firm whose identity is verified (src:15009)
GIVEN a IS A `s 1067A(2) facts about the individual who delivers the document (A)`
      statements IS A LIST OF `s 1067A(2) statement made by A`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1067A(2) row 1 is satisfied` MEANS
    `s 1067A(2) the plain facts hold and the answer of another section is`
        (       a's `s 1067A(2) A is an officer or employee of the firm`
           AND  elem `s 1067A(2) statement that A is an officer or employee of the firm` statements
           AND  elem `s 1067A(2) statement that A is delivering the document on the firm's behalf` statements
           AND  elem `s 1067A(2) statement that A's identity is verified` statements)
        (a's `s 1067A(2) A's identity is verified, the answer of section 1110A`)

-- src:15010 | 2 | Firm | Individual who is an officer or employee of a corporate officer of the firm and whose identity is verified. | Statement by A—that A is an officer or employee of a corporate officer of the firm,that A is delivering the document on the firm’s behalf, andthat A’s identity is verified.
@ref s 1067A(2) Table row 2: a firm; an officer or employee of a corporate officer of the firm whose identity is verified (src:15010)
GIVEN a IS A `s 1067A(2) facts about the individual who delivers the document (A)`
      statements IS A LIST OF `s 1067A(2) statement made by A`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1067A(2) row 2 is satisfied` MEANS
    `s 1067A(2) the plain facts hold and the answer of another section is`
        (       a's `s 1067A(2) A is an officer or employee of a corporate officer of the firm`
           AND  elem `s 1067A(2) statement that A is an officer or employee of a corporate officer of the firm` statements
           AND  elem `s 1067A(2) statement that A is delivering the document on the firm's behalf` statements
           AND  elem `s 1067A(2) statement that A's identity is verified` statements)
        (a's `s 1067A(2) A's identity is verified, the answer of section 1110A`)

-- src:15011 | 3 | Firm | Individual who is an authorised corporate service provider (see section 1098A). | Statement by A—that A is an authorised corporate service provider, andthat A is delivering the document on the firm’s behalf.
@ref s 1067A(2) Table row 3: a firm; an individual who is an authorised corporate service provider (src:15011)
GIVEN a IS A `s 1067A(2) facts about the individual who delivers the document (A)`
      statements IS A LIST OF `s 1067A(2) statement made by A`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1067A(2) row 3 is satisfied` MEANS
    `s 1067A(2) the plain facts hold and the answer of another section is`
        (       elem `s 1067A(2) statement that A is an authorised corporate service provider` statements
           AND  elem `s 1067A(2) statement that A is delivering the document on the firm's behalf` statements)
        (a's `s 1067A(2) A is an authorised corporate service provider, the answer of section 1098A`)

-- src:15012 | 4 | Firm | Individual who is an officer or employee of an authorised corporate service provider. | Statement by A—that A is an officer or employee of an authorised corporate service provider, andthat A is delivering the document on the firm’s behalf.
@ref s 1067A(2) Table row 4: a firm; an officer or employee of an authorised corporate service provider (src:15012)
GIVEN a IS A `s 1067A(2) facts about the individual who delivers the document (A)`
      statements IS A LIST OF `s 1067A(2) statement made by A`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1067A(2) row 4 is satisfied` MEANS
    IF       a's `s 1067A(2) A is an officer or employee of an authorised corporate service provider`
        AND  elem `s 1067A(2) statement that A is an officer or employee of an authorised corporate service provider` statements
        AND  elem `s 1067A(2) statement that A is delivering the document on the firm's behalf` statements
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the row is an exception stated by "unless (a) ... and (b) ...", and a limb that fails is a no (marginal reading (a))

-- src:15013 | 5 | Individual | Individual whose identity is verified. | Statement by A—that A is delivering the document on B’s behalf, andthat A’s identity is verified.
@ref s 1067A(2) Table row 5: an individual; an individual whose identity is verified (src:15013)
GIVEN a IS A `s 1067A(2) facts about the individual who delivers the document (A)`
      statements IS A LIST OF `s 1067A(2) statement made by A`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1067A(2) row 5 is satisfied` MEANS
    `s 1067A(2) the plain facts hold and the answer of another section is`
        (       elem `s 1067A(2) statement that A is delivering the document on B's behalf` statements
           AND  elem `s 1067A(2) statement that A's identity is verified` statements)
        (a's `s 1067A(2) A's identity is verified, the answer of section 1110A`)

-- src:15014 | 6 | Individual | Individual who is an authorised corporate service provider. | Statement by A—that A is an authorised corporate service provider, andthat A is delivering the document on B’s behalf.
@ref s 1067A(2) Table row 6: an individual; an individual who is an authorised corporate service provider (src:15014)
GIVEN a IS A `s 1067A(2) facts about the individual who delivers the document (A)`
      statements IS A LIST OF `s 1067A(2) statement made by A`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1067A(2) row 6 is satisfied` MEANS
    `s 1067A(2) the plain facts hold and the answer of another section is`
        (       elem `s 1067A(2) statement that A is an authorised corporate service provider` statements
           AND  elem `s 1067A(2) statement that A is delivering the document on B's behalf` statements)
        (a's `s 1067A(2) A is an authorised corporate service provider, the answer of section 1098A`)

-- src:15015 | 7 | Individual | Individual who is an officer or employee of an authorised corporate service provider. | Statement by A—that A is an officer or employee of an authorised corporate service provider, andthat A is delivering the document on B’s behalf.
@ref s 1067A(2) Table row 7: an individual; an officer or employee of an authorised corporate service provider (src:15015)
GIVEN a IS A `s 1067A(2) facts about the individual who delivers the document (A)`
      statements IS A LIST OF `s 1067A(2) statement made by A`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1067A(2) row 7 is satisfied` MEANS
    IF       a's `s 1067A(2) A is an officer or employee of an authorised corporate service provider`
        AND  elem `s 1067A(2) statement that A is an officer or employee of an authorised corporate service provider` statements
        AND  elem `s 1067A(2) statement that A is delivering the document on B's behalf` statements
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the row is an exception stated by "unless (a) and (b)", and a limb that fails is a no (marginal reading (a))

-- Any row satisfied lifts the bar; otherwise a row that cannot be decided leaves the question open; otherwise the bar applies.
-- src:15004 | (2) An individual (A) may not deliver a document to the registrar on behalf of another person (B) who is of a description specified in column 1 of the following table unless—
-- src:15005 | (a) the individual is of a description specified in the corresponding entry in column 2, and
-- src:15006 | (b) the document is accompanied by the statement specified in the corresponding entry in column 3.
@ref s 1067A(2) An individual delivering a document on behalf of another person (src:15004-15006)
GIVEN b IS A `s 1067A(2) the person on whose behalf the document is delivered (B)`
      a IS A `s 1067A(2) facts about the individual who delivers the document (A)`
      statements IS A LIST OF `s 1067A(2) statement made by A`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1067A(2) the individual is barred from delivering the document to the registrar on behalf of B` MEANS
    CONSIDER b
    WHEN `s 1067A(2) B is a firm` THEN
        `s 1067A(2) the bar applies unless one of the rows is satisfied`
            (LIST `s 1067A(2) row 1 is satisfied` a statements
                , `s 1067A(2) row 2 is satisfied` a statements
                , `s 1067A(2) row 3 is satisfied` a statements
                , `s 1067A(2) row 4 is satisfied` a statements)
    WHEN `s 1067A(2) B is an individual` THEN
        `s 1067A(2) the bar applies unless one of the rows is satisfied`
            (LIST `s 1067A(2) row 5 is satisfied` a statements
                , `s 1067A(2) row 6 is satisfied` a statements
                , `s 1067A(2) row 7 is satisfied` a statements)

@ref s 1067A(2) The bar applies unless one of B's rows is satisfied (src:15004-15006)
GIVEN rows IS A LIST OF MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1067A(2) the bar applies unless one of the rows is satisfied` MEANS
    IF elem (JUST TRUE) rows
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An individual (A) may not deliver a document ... unless— (a) ... and (b) ..." (an "unless" once met: fork F9)
    ELSE IF elem NOTHING rows
         THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): a row turns on section 1110A or section 1098A, in another part's range (coa24)
         ELSE JUST TRUE

DECLARE `s 1067A(3) level of officers` HAS
    `s 1067A(3) the level has at least one individual who is an officer` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 1067A(3) the individual is an officer at this level` IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:15016 | (3) In relation to a corporate officer that has only corporate officers, the reference in row 2 of the table to an individual who is one of its officers is to—
-- src:15017 | (a) an individual who is an officer of one of those corporate officers, or
-- src:15018 | (b) if the officers of those corporate officers are all corporate officers, an individual who is an officer of any of the corporate officers’ corporate officers,
-- src:15019 | and so on until there is at least one individual who is an officer.
@ref s 1067A(3) A corporate officer that has only corporate officers (src:15016-15019)
GIVEN `the levels of officers, the corporate officer's own officers first` IS A LIST OF `s 1067A(3) level of officers`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1067A(3) the individual is one of the officers of the corporate officer for the purposes of row 2` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the levels of officers, the corporate officer's own officers first`
    WHEN EMPTY THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): no individual is an officer at any level, so "and so on until there is at least one individual who is an officer" never ends
    WHEN level FOLLOWED BY deeper THEN
        IF level's `s 1067A(3) the level has at least one individual who is an officer`
        THEN JUST (level's `s 1067A(3) the individual is an officer at this level`)
        ELSE `s 1067A(3) the individual is one of the officers of the corporate officer for the purposes of row 2` deeper

-- src:15028 | (8) In this section “corporate officer” means an officer that is not an individual.
@ref s 1067A(8) "corporate officer" (src:15028)
GIVEN `the officer is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1067A(8) the officer is a corporate officer` MEANS
    IF `the officer is an individual`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“corporate officer” means an officer that is not an individual"
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- s 1067A(4), (5), (6) and (7) confer powers to make regulations, or fix their procedure: inert (reason 2).

-- src:15030 | (1) An individual who is a disqualified person may not deliver documents to the registrar on their own behalf or on behalf of another.
@ref s 1067B(1) A disqualified person may not deliver documents (src:15030)
GIVEN `the individual is a disqualified person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1067B(1) the individual is barred from delivering documents to the registrar on their own behalf or on behalf of another` MEANS
    IF `the individual is a disqualified person`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An individual who is a disqualified person may not deliver documents" (a prohibition limited by its own wording: marginal reading (b))

-- The bar as a regulative rule: any act of delivering, by the disqualified individual, is a breach. No time limit is stated.
@ref s 1067B(1) The bar as a prohibition (src:15030)
`s 1067B(1) the prohibition on a disqualified individual delivering documents` MEANS
    PARTY `s 1067A an individual who delivers a document to the registrar`
    SHANT `s 1067B deliver documents on their own behalf or on behalf of another as a disqualified person`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `s 1067A an individual who delivers a document to the registrar` BECAUSE "a disqualified person delivered documents to the registrar"

-- src:15031 | (2) An individual may not deliver a document to the registrar on behalf of a disqualified person unless—
-- src:15032 | (a) the individual is an authorised corporate service provider (see section 1098A), or
-- src:15033 | (b) the individual is an officer or employee of an authorised corporate service provider.
@ref s 1067B(2) Delivering a document on behalf of a disqualified person (src:15031-15033)
GIVEN `the document is delivered on behalf of a disqualified person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 1098A the individual is an authorised corporate service provider` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the individual is an officer or employee of an authorised corporate service provider` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1067B(2) the individual is barred from delivering the document to the registrar on behalf of the disqualified person` MEANS
    IF `the document is delivered on behalf of a disqualified person`
    THEN IF `the individual is an officer or employee of an authorised corporate service provider`
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An individual may not deliver a document ... on behalf of a disqualified person unless ... (b) the individual is an officer or employee of an authorised corporate service provider" (an "unless" once met: fork F9)
         ELSE CONSIDER `s 1098A the individual is an authorised corporate service provider`
              WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless— (a) the individual is an authorised corporate service provider" (an "unless" once met: fork F9)
              WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST TRUE
              WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the individual is an authorised corporate service provider is section 1098A, in another part's range (coa24)
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the bar is on delivering "on behalf of a disqualified person" (marginal reading (b))

DECLARE `s 1067B(5) the second statement` IS ONE OF
    `s 1067B(5)(a) a statement that the individual is delivering the document on their own behalf`
    `s 1067B(5)(b) a statement that the individual is delivering the document on behalf of another person who is not a disqualified person`
    `s 1067B(5)(c) a statement that the individual is delivering the document on behalf of a disqualified person`
    `s 1067B(5) no second statement`

-- src:15034 | (3) A document delivered to the registrar must be accompanied by the following two statements made by the individual delivering it.
-- src:15035 | (4) The first is a statement that the individual is not a disqualified person.
-- src:15036 | (5) The second is—
-- src:15037 | (a) a statement that the individual is delivering the document on their own behalf,
-- src:15038 | (b) a statement that the individual is delivering the document on behalf of another person who is not a disqualified person, or
-- src:15039 | (c) a statement that the individual is delivering the document on behalf of a disqualified person.
@ref s 1067B(3) to (5) The two statements that must accompany a document (src:15034-15039)
