      `the second statement that accompanies the document` IS A `s 1067B(5) the second statement`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1067B(3) the document is accompanied by the two statements` MEANS
    IF `the first statement that the individual is not a disqualified person accompanies the document`
    THEN CONSIDER `the second statement that accompanies the document`
         WHEN `s 1067B(5) no second statement` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A document delivered to the registrar must be accompanied by the following two statements" (a bare "must" not done: fork F5)
         OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A document delivered to the registrar must be accompanied by the following two statements ... The first is a statement that the individual is not a disqualified person" (a bare "must" not done: fork F5)

-- src:15040 | (6) For the purpose of this section “disqualified person” means a person who is disqualified under the directors disqualification legislation (see section 159A(2)).
@ref s 1067B(6) "disqualified person" (src:15040)
