    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the borrowed definition says no, supplied as an input): "“disqualified person” means a person who is disqualified under the directors disqualification legislation"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): section 159A(2) is in another part's range (coa4)

