§§ `ss 1068 to 1071 Delivery of documents to the registrar`

DECLARE `s 1068 head of requirement` IS ONE OF
    `s 1068(2)(a) that the contents of the document be in a standard form`
    `s 1068(2)(b) requirements for the purpose of enabling the document to be scanned or copied`
    `s 1068(3)(a) that the document be authenticated by a particular person or a person of a particular description`
    `s 1068(3)(b) the means of authentication`
    `s 1068(3)(c) that the document contain or be accompanied by the name or registered number (or both) of the company (or other body) to which it relates`
    `s 1068(4)(a) the physical form of the document`
    `s 1068(4)(b) the means to be used for delivering the document`
    `s 1068(4)(c) the address to which the document is to be sent`
    `s 1068(4)(d) the hardware and software to be used, and technical specifications, for a document delivered by electronic means`
    `s 1068 another requirement`

-- src:15045 | (1) The registrar may impose requirements as to the form, authentication and manner of delivery of documents required or authorised to be delivered to the registrar under any enactment.
-- src:15046 | (2) As regards the form of the document, the registrar may—
-- src:15047 | (a) require the contents of the document to be in a standard form;
-- src:15048 | (b) impose requirements for the purpose of enabling the document to be scanned or copied.
-- src:15049 | (3) As regards authentication, the registrar may—
-- src:15050 | (a) require the document to be authenticated by a particular person or a person of a particular description;
-- src:15051 | (b) specify the means of authentication;
-- src:15052 | (c) require the document to contain or be accompanied by the name or registered number (or both) of the company (or other body) to which it relates.
-- src:15053 | (4) As regards the manner of delivery, the registrar may specify requirements as to—
-- src:15054 | (a) the physical form of the document (for example, hard copy or electronic form);
-- src:15055 | (b) the means to be used for delivering the document (for example, by post or electronic means);
-- src:15056 | (c) the address to which the document is to be sent;
-- src:15057 | (d) in the case of a document to be delivered by electronic means, the hardware and software to be used, and technical specifications (for example, matters relating to protocol, security, anti-virus protection or encryption).
@ref s 1068(1) to (4) Registrar's requirements as to form, authentication and manner of delivery (src:15045-15057)
GIVEN h IS A `s 1068 head of requirement`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1068 the registrar may impose the requirement` MEANS
    CONSIDER h
    WHEN `s 1068 another requirement` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the heads in subsections (2) to (4) are examples of "the form, authentication and manner of delivery" and are not closed with "only"
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:15058 | (4A) Any requirements under subsection (4)(b) to (d) must be imposed by means of registrar’s rules.
@ref s 1068(4A) Requirements under subsection (4)(b) to (d) are imposed by registrar's rules (src:15058)
GIVEN h IS A `s 1068 head of requirement`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1068(4A) the requirement must be imposed by means of registrar's rules` MEANS
    CONSIDER h
    WHEN `s 1068(4)(b) the means to be used for delivering the document` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 1068(4)(c) the address to which the document is to be sent` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 1068(4)(d) the hardware and software to be used, and technical specifications, for a document delivered by electronic means` THEN JUST TRUE
    OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any requirements under subsection (4)(b) to (d) must be imposed by means of registrar’s rules" says nothing of the other heads

-- s 1068(5), (6) and (6A) are blank in this text.

