    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty is on "Documents in relation to which an agreement is in force"

-- The duty as a regulative rule. The text names no deliverer, so the company (the party to the agreement) is taken (fork F11); no time limit is stated.
@ref s 1070(3) The duty to deliver in accordance with the agreement (src:15076)
`s 1070(3) the duty to deliver in accordance with the agreement` MEANS
    PARTY Company
    MUST `Action of a party` OF Company, Registrar, "deliver the document in accordance with the agreement"

-- src:15078 | (1) A document is not delivered to the registrar until it is received by the registrar.
@ref s 1071(1) A document is not delivered until it is received (src:15078)
GIVEN `the registrar has received the document` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1071(1) the document cannot yet count as delivered to the registrar` MEANS
